-- title:
--   Level-ℓ Hecke sets of nested orders agreeing at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra. Let $\Lambda, S, R$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{H}$, each an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and with $\mathbb{Q}$-span all of $\mathbb{H}$. Assume $S\le R\le\Lambda$. Let $\ell$ be a nonzero natural number, and assume that for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains $\ell$ one has [`Submodule.localBox S v = Submodule.localBox R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), where [`Submodule.localBox O v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$. Let $\beta$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose component [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) at every height-one prime $v$ not containing $\ell$ equals $1$. Then $\beta$ lies in [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet Λ S ℓ`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) if and only if it lies in [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44); here, for an order $O$, this set consists of those units $h$ such that $h$ and $\ell\cdot h^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox O`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) while $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot h$ do not (the condition [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet O ℓ`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109)), such that the order $\mathbb{H}\cap h\widehat{O}h^{-1}$ given by [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele O h`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) differs from $O$, and such that $O$ is not contained in $\mathbb{H}\cap h\widehat{\Lambda}h^{-1}$.
--
--   The level-$\ell$ Hecke condition defining the $U_\ell$-type sets attached to a pair of nested quaternion orders is insensitive, on idèles concentrated at $\ell$, to replacing one order by another with the same completions at the primes above $\ell$. It is used in the computation of the Hecke matrix on the class-set graph, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.pushforward_classSetHeckeMatrix_levelHeckeUSet_meetOrder_mulVecLin`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.pushforward_classSetHeckeMatrix_levelHeckeUSet_meetOrder_mulVecLin).
